WEBVTT

00:01.857 --> 00:03.525
<i>Previously on</i> Lost:

00:03.609 --> 00:04.777
Is that a helicopter?

00:04.860 --> 00:07.269
Is that how a helicopter's
supposed to sound?

00:07.363 --> 00:09.907
Get away from her!

00:10.532 --> 00:12.368
Desmond.

00:14.703 --> 00:15.871
What's wrong?

00:15.954 --> 00:18.196
- What's wrong is I'm married.
- Right.

00:33.764 --> 00:35.265
You're pregnant.

01:04.294 --> 01:06.004
Hey.

01:06.964 --> 01:08.924
Good morning, Jack.

01:09.007 --> 01:10.968
Need a hand?

01:11.051 --> 01:13.043
Thank you.

01:19.018 --> 01:22.552
I came by your tent earlier.

01:22.646 --> 01:23.981
Is Jin gone?

01:25.357 --> 01:28.444
He went off with Charlie,
Hurley, and Desmond.

01:28.527 --> 01:31.572
- Did you need him?
- Actually, I was looking for you.

01:31.655 --> 01:35.659
I wanted to see how you were doing
with your pregnancy.

01:38.078 --> 01:42.541
I'm doing fine. A little tired,
but that's normal, right?

01:42.624 --> 01:47.171
- Sure. Any morning sickness?
- Not anymore.

01:48.422 --> 01:50.799
Any bleeding?

01:53.594 --> 01:56.169
Why are you asking me
all these questions, Jack?

01:58.098 --> 01:59.433
I'm just checking in.

02:00.517 --> 02:04.646
Now that I'm back, I just wanted
to make sure that you were doing OK.

02:05.898 --> 02:08.567
Thank you. I'm OK.

02:09.610 --> 02:10.694
Great.

04:39.843 --> 04:41.428
- Who is she?
- I've no idea.

04:41.512 --> 04:44.556
She seems to know you, dude.
She just said your name.

04:44.640 --> 04:46.684
I've never seen her before in my life.

04:48.686 --> 04:50.104
She's waking up.

04:52.898 --> 04:55.609
She's trying to talk.
We should get her some water.

04:56.944 --> 04:58.935
- Give me a hand.
- Yeah.

05:03.033 --> 05:05.327
- What's she saying?
- Don't know.

05:05.411 --> 05:08.914
- It's Spanish, dude.
- Do you understand her, then?

05:13.043 --> 05:14.326
She says she's dying.

05:20.592 --> 05:21.593
Oh, my God!

05:21.677 --> 05:24.002
A branch.
She must have hit it on the way down.

05:24.096 --> 05:27.516
Get her pack. We haven't
got much in this first-aid kit.

05:27.599 --> 05:30.884
- See if there's anything we can use.
- What if this is a rescue?

05:30.978 --> 05:33.470
What if she came for us?
Is she gonna be OK?

05:33.564 --> 05:35.941
Just go. Start looking.

05:39.403 --> 05:43.866
- We get Jack. Jack.
- She could be our way off the island.

05:43.949 --> 05:47.536
- If we move her, it'll make it worse.
- We just let her bleed to death?

05:47.619 --> 05:51.457
- No, we need to bring Jack here.
- It's an eight-hour walk, one way.

05:51.540 --> 05:54.334
- Then I'll run.
- Are you out of your mind?

05:54.418 --> 05:57.588
It's not safe.
Who knows who's out in this jungle?

05:57.671 --> 06:00.132
People on this island
are trying to kill us.

06:00.215 --> 06:02.259
Nobody knows we're here.

06:16.440 --> 06:17.639
Oops.

08:09.456 --> 08:13.627
- How's this?
- That's perfect. Thank you.

08:21.135 --> 08:24.721
What do you think happened to Jack
while he was with the Others?

08:25.848 --> 08:28.767
Since he's been back,
he seems different.

08:31.019 --> 08:33.261
He says that he was
pretty much a prisoner,

08:33.355 --> 08:37.776
and he only cooperated 'cause he thought
they'd let him off the island.

08:39.361 --> 08:41.353
Do you believe him?

08:43.157 --> 08:45.148
Why wouldn't I?

08:46.368 --> 08:49.329
He came to me,
asking about my pregnancy.

08:50.664 --> 08:53.751
- What would that have anything to do...
- What if...

08:53.834 --> 08:55.961
What if the Others want my baby?

08:56.920 --> 08:59.047
He's been there alone for over a week.

08:59.131 --> 09:01.967
How do we know
he isn't working with them?

09:06.430 --> 09:08.922
He's not working with them.

09:10.934 --> 09:13.426
Do you know something, Kate?

09:22.029 --> 09:24.020
It's Juliet.

09:24.114 --> 09:28.066
She was their doctor, their fertility
doctor, studying pregnant women.

09:28.160 --> 09:32.706
And when Claire was sick,
she told me and Jack

09:32.790 --> 09:37.127
the reason the Others wanted her baby
was for research.

09:44.426 --> 09:46.386
Sun. Wait. You don't have to do this.

09:46.470 --> 09:48.461
Go away, Kate.

09:50.599 --> 09:53.519
I want to know about your research.

09:53.602 --> 09:56.522
- Sun...
- What happens to pregnant women?

09:58.649 --> 10:00.640
You're pregnant?

10:00.734 --> 10:04.488
- Are you sure? How do you know?
- I asked you a question.

10:04.571 --> 10:08.700
Everyone might be all right with you
washing your clothes, eating our food.

10:08.784 --> 10:12.736
But I want to know what's going on.
I want answers.

10:14.289 --> 10:17.574
What are you people doing?
Why are you taking children?

10:19.753 --> 10:22.923
What happens to pregnant women
on this island?

10:24.258 --> 10:26.802
- What happens...
- They die.

10:28.846 --> 10:31.306
They all die.

10:33.559 --> 10:35.550
Sun, come on. Let's go.

10:45.571 --> 10:49.189
- What's she saying?
- Chinese, not Korean.

10:49.283 --> 10:51.994
- Maybe we should pull it out.
- You'll make it worse.

10:52.077 --> 10:55.247
Have you forgotten what's at stake,
or is this another flash?

10:55.330 --> 10:59.334
- Who's getting an arrow in the neck?
- Lest you forget, she said my name.

11:00.627 --> 11:03.119
She had a photo of me
and my girlfriend.

11:04.173 --> 11:06.248
I understand better than the lot of you.

11:06.341 --> 11:08.500
Hey, guys, chill.

11:08.594 --> 11:11.430
We've wasted enough time already.

11:11.513 --> 11:13.891
- You're not leaving us.
- Get out of my way.

11:13.974 --> 11:15.559
No.

11:46.131 --> 11:47.633
Hey, Jin! Jin!

11:47.716 --> 11:49.259
Jin!

12:35.973 --> 12:36.974
Who are you?

12:38.809 --> 12:40.967
I said, who are you?

12:43.105 --> 12:45.649
He's the guy who shot Sayid.

12:45.732 --> 12:50.362
Kate told us he lived out in that
station Locke blew up. He's an Other.

12:50.446 --> 12:54.283
I thought Locke killed that guy
with the electro-fence thingy.

12:54.366 --> 12:58.203
You've got five seconds to talk
or I fire this gun, brother.

13:00.289 --> 13:01.457
That's a flare gun.

13:01.540 --> 13:03.208
And how do you think it'll feel

13:03.292 --> 13:06.743
taking a flare to the chest
at this range?

13:08.005 --> 13:11.091
As your friend pointed out,
I already died once this week.

13:18.891 --> 13:22.425
- You understand her.
- She's speaking Italian.

13:22.519 --> 13:25.189
She said she's dying.
She needs help.

13:26.899 --> 13:30.402
I was a Soviet army field medic.
I can offer you my services.

13:31.612 --> 13:34.281
- Wait. What are you doing?
- I'm saving her.

13:42.623 --> 13:45.876
This branch has punctured her lung.
It's filling with blood.

13:45.959 --> 13:49.046
If it is not ventilated soon,
she is going to die.

13:53.175 --> 13:55.167
Well, do it. Help her.

13:55.260 --> 13:59.515
If I fix her, you must let me walk away
as if I never came upon you.

14:08.440 --> 14:10.432
What do you need?

18:01.673 --> 18:04.468
Be quiet. Don't move.

18:05.594 --> 18:09.045
You want me to help you
and your baby, I have answers.

18:09.139 --> 18:11.381
But you have to
come with me right now.

18:11.475 --> 18:14.311
Just you and me. Nobody else.

18:21.276 --> 18:25.145
If what you said was true,
that means I'm already dead.

18:25.239 --> 18:29.243
- Why should I go anywhere with you?
- Because there may be hope for you yet.

18:54.977 --> 18:56.937
Where are we going?

18:57.020 --> 19:00.305
There's a medical station.
They have an ultrasound machine.

19:00.399 --> 19:04.184
Claire and Kate
told me about that place.

19:04.278 --> 19:06.655
It was abandoned.
They found nothing there.

19:06.738 --> 19:09.533
Well, that's because
they didn't know where to look.

19:10.200 --> 19:12.661
What are you going to do to me?

19:16.206 --> 19:19.376
I'm gonna look at your baby
and determine the DOC.

19:19.460 --> 19:20.878
Date of conception.

19:20.961 --> 19:24.496
The ultrasound will tell me when
you got pregnant, give or take a day.

19:24.590 --> 19:29.219
If you got pregnant off the island, then
you and your baby will probably be OK.

19:30.137 --> 19:33.421
But if you got pregnant here...

19:35.434 --> 19:38.771
We'll cross that bridge
when we come to it.

19:38.854 --> 19:42.024
When was the last time
you and your husband had sex?

19:42.107 --> 19:45.444
- I would rather not talk about that.
- I know it's personal.

19:45.527 --> 19:49.782
- But if I know when, I can figure...
- Isn't that what the machine will do?

19:49.865 --> 19:53.786
- Yeah.
- Then let's keep walking.

22:59.096 --> 23:02.933
What do you know about her? Did she
have anything besides the flare gun?

23:03.016 --> 23:06.145
Just a book, a fancy radio phone thingy.

23:08.814 --> 23:11.483
Does it work?

23:11.567 --> 23:13.777
Like I'd tell you.

23:13.861 --> 23:18.240
One of you must help.
The rest, clear the way. I need space.

23:18.323 --> 23:20.451
I'll do it.

23:22.077 --> 23:25.080
Wipe away as much of the blood
as you can.

23:25.164 --> 23:27.791
We need to evacuate the air now.

23:27.875 --> 23:29.835
Hold her steady.

23:29.918 --> 23:32.212
- Steady!
- Yeah, I heard you.

23:37.676 --> 23:39.511
Is that normal?

23:46.643 --> 23:48.635
Gauze.

23:51.106 --> 23:56.153
Tape it. Be careful.
The covering needs to be hollow.

23:56.236 --> 23:58.562
The wound needs to breathe.

24:05.454 --> 24:07.863
What did she say?

24:07.956 --> 24:09.124
"Thank you."

24:10.250 --> 24:12.576
She said, "Thank you for helping me."

24:23.514 --> 24:25.505
It's right down here.

25:23.282 --> 25:25.857
Why are you doing this?

25:25.951 --> 25:26.952
What?

25:28.078 --> 25:29.663
Helping me.

25:39.715 --> 25:42.040
Once upon a time,

25:42.134 --> 25:45.888
I told women that they were pregnant,

25:45.971 --> 25:49.506
and their faces...

25:49.600 --> 25:54.563
It was the best news
they ever got in their entire life.

25:56.482 --> 25:59.193
Then I came here.

26:01.612 --> 26:03.822
I've lost...

26:04.865 --> 26:08.869
...nine patients
in the last three years.

26:12.956 --> 26:15.448
I'm helping you
because I want to tell you

26:15.542 --> 26:19.296
that you and your husband
got pregnant before you came here.

26:23.926 --> 26:26.887
I'm helping you because
I want to give good news again.

26:33.852 --> 26:36.344
I slept with another man.

26:40.192 --> 26:42.027
Before we got to the island.

26:46.073 --> 26:48.064
Jin and I, we were having...

26:50.536 --> 26:51.818
...trouble.

26:51.912 --> 26:53.904
We weren't...

26:58.335 --> 27:00.879
And I had a friend.

27:08.929 --> 27:10.921
It was a mistake.

27:11.014 --> 27:13.225
We all make mistakes.

27:17.771 --> 27:18.887
Which way?

27:54.099 --> 27:56.591
Will you help me move this forward?

28:29.760 --> 28:32.252
Why is this room hidden?

28:34.264 --> 28:37.059
- Don't worry about it.
- What is this place?

28:39.853 --> 28:41.480
Tell me.

28:44.066 --> 28:46.985
It's where we brought the women to die.

28:52.491 --> 28:56.703
She's fine. Keep the wound
as clean as you can.

28:57.913 --> 29:02.543
- She should be better in a day.
- A day? Her lung was punctured.

29:04.378 --> 29:07.339
On this island,
the rules are a bit different.

29:07.423 --> 29:08.882
Maybe a day and a half.

29:14.638 --> 29:18.507
I did as I promised. She will live.

29:18.600 --> 29:21.092
- You're considering letting him go?
- Just go.

29:23.856 --> 29:26.817
- He's one of them.
- So what would you have me do, Charlie?

29:26.900 --> 29:30.654
We've got to make a stretcher and
carry her. How do we bring a prisoner?

29:30.737 --> 29:34.689
- I'll take responsibility.
- Phone. Phone!

29:35.617 --> 29:36.952
- No, Jin!
- Phone!

29:37.035 --> 29:39.496
- Jin, it's all right.
- No, let him, Desmond.

29:39.580 --> 29:41.571
Let him!

29:42.708 --> 29:44.950
Jin, it's all right! Jin!

29:45.043 --> 29:47.796
Let him go. Jin, let him go!

29:47.880 --> 29:49.079
Phone!

29:56.555 --> 29:57.838
You stole this?

29:57.931 --> 30:00.006
How could you respect me
if I didn't try?

30:00.100 --> 30:03.187
How about I take your other eye?
Would you respect that?

30:03.270 --> 30:05.314
Sorry. What?

30:06.607 --> 30:10.475
- Charlie, don't! Charlie, let him go!
- This is a mistake.

30:10.569 --> 30:14.907
- We can't keep letting these people go.
- We gave him our word.

30:23.957 --> 30:26.585
Go on. Get out of here.

30:49.566 --> 30:51.151
The baby isn't Jin's.

30:55.531 --> 30:58.367
We tried to have a baby
back in Korea and couldn't.

30:58.450 --> 31:00.442
And the doctor...

31:04.123 --> 31:06.834
He told me Jin was infertile.

31:06.917 --> 31:10.337
- And then you came here.
- What?

31:11.547 --> 31:14.800
Did you know
that the average male sperm count

31:14.883 --> 31:18.220
is between 60 and 80 million?

31:20.222 --> 31:23.642
But on this island,
it's five times that.

31:23.725 --> 31:25.769
We call that good odds.

31:28.814 --> 31:30.774
You ready?

31:32.025 --> 31:34.945
- Yes.
- OK. Wanna lift up your shirt a little?

31:36.822 --> 31:38.813
It's cold.

31:41.326 --> 31:43.454
- Will I see the baby?
- Maybe.

31:43.537 --> 31:47.458
It's your first trimester,
so it's a little iffy.

31:47.541 --> 31:52.838
If you don't see a heartbeat,
don't worry about it, it's just early.

31:54.214 --> 31:56.175
How does it work?

31:56.258 --> 31:58.802
Well, I take a measurement of the fetus,

31:58.886 --> 32:02.723
and that will tell us
when your baby was conceived.

32:03.974 --> 32:05.966
And then we'll know who.

32:10.022 --> 32:11.982
You OK?

32:13.650 --> 32:15.642
I lose either way.

32:17.321 --> 32:22.659
If I'm going to live,
that means the baby's not Jin's.

32:24.536 --> 32:26.163
Do you still wanna do this?

32:28.874 --> 32:29.990
Yes.

32:31.085 --> 32:34.755
OK. The moment of truth.

35:20.087 --> 35:23.371
There it is. There's your baby.

35:23.465 --> 35:25.457
You see?

35:29.555 --> 35:31.546
I can see it.

35:34.393 --> 35:37.980
- Is it a boy or a girl?
- It's a little early.

35:38.063 --> 35:41.900
But do you see that little flutter?

35:44.194 --> 35:46.238
That's the heart beating.

35:50.576 --> 35:53.745
It's very strong. It's very healthy.

35:58.751 --> 36:00.335
OK.

36:01.044 --> 36:04.006
You crashed here 90 days ago.

36:05.716 --> 36:11.722
The baby was conceived
about eight weeks ago, so 53 days.

36:16.059 --> 36:18.353
You got pregnant on the island.

36:22.399 --> 36:25.611
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry, Sun.

36:25.694 --> 36:28.697
I will do everything that I can.

36:39.666 --> 36:41.418
It's Jin's.

38:17.264 --> 38:19.756
So how long do I have?

38:21.435 --> 38:26.179
Most of the women made it into
the middle of their second trimester.

38:28.108 --> 38:29.693
Nobody made to their third.

38:32.529 --> 38:34.573
That gives me two months.

38:38.911 --> 38:40.902
I am...

38:44.291 --> 38:46.616
...very happy the baby is Jin's.

38:47.878 --> 38:49.870
You gave me good news, Juliet.

38:52.299 --> 38:54.426
It was my pleasure, Sun.

38:56.512 --> 39:00.130
I'm gonna go back inside
and make sure I didn't miss anything.

39:00.224 --> 39:03.560
I don't wanna take the chance
that we didn't cover our tracks.

39:07.523 --> 39:09.066
Do you wanna wait out here?

39:10.526 --> 39:12.517
All right.

39:16.115 --> 39:17.991
Juliet.

39:19.868 --> 39:21.120
Thank you.

39:56.321 --> 39:58.615
Ben, it's 6 AM on Saturday morning.

40:00.993 --> 40:02.536
Kwon is pregnant.

40:02.619 --> 40:06.457
The fetus is healthy and was conceived
on island with her husband.

40:06.540 --> 40:08.500
He was sterile before they got here.

40:08.584 --> 40:11.545
Still working on getting samples
from the other women.

40:11.628 --> 40:15.716
I should have Austen's soon.
I'll report back when I know more.

40:22.723 --> 40:24.714
I hate you.

40:31.398 --> 40:33.974
You can't trust them, you know.

40:34.067 --> 40:36.195
- What's that?
- The Others.

40:36.278 --> 40:40.365
The one you let go, he'll be back
tomorrow with five of his mates.

40:40.449 --> 40:43.076
We should've killed him.

40:43.160 --> 40:46.330
- Charlie. Tight.
- OK.

40:46.413 --> 40:48.874
You know, brother,

40:48.957 --> 40:54.338
by my count, you've killed more of them
than they've killed of you.

40:54.421 --> 40:57.706
They started it. Just 'cause
one comes back with Jack and Kate

40:57.800 --> 40:59.875
doesn't mean that we can trust them now.

41:21.365 --> 41:23.356
Mom?

41:26.578 --> 41:28.622
Where am I?

41:29.373 --> 41:31.250
- You had a branch...
- Where am I?

41:31.333 --> 41:33.710
I don't know.

41:33.794 --> 41:37.078
You're on an island.
Are you here to rescue us?

41:37.172 --> 41:39.842
Are there more of you?
Can you make your phone work?

41:39.925 --> 41:42.250
- Who are you?
- Hugo Reyes.

41:42.344 --> 41:45.931
I crashed here on Oceanic Flight 815.
A bunch of us survived.

41:46.014 --> 41:48.934
Is that why you're here?
Were you looking for us?

41:49.852 --> 41:52.229
815?

41:52.312 --> 41:54.940
Flight 815? The one from Sydney?

41:55.023 --> 41:56.650
Yeah.

41:57.234 --> 41:59.361
No. That's not possible.

41:59.445 --> 42:03.574
Yeah, I know. It wasn't easy, but we
found food and a hatch and more food...

42:03.657 --> 42:07.161
Flight 815... They...
They found the plane.

42:09.455 --> 42:11.446
There were no survivors.

42:15.085 --> 42:16.117
They were all dead.

42:21.383 --> 42:22.551
What?
